#
# schema 2 exists because schema 1 was edited in place. the merge that made
# 30-root shipped by rewriting the v1 rows rather than adding new ones, so a
# state file already stamped 1 had the OLD table applied and never sees the
# new one -- migrate() bails when want <= cur. those installs are sitting on
# 31-root and 30-proving-this-machine, two ids no level file answers to. a
# version of their own is the only thing that reaches them; on a state file
# still at 0 both rows are no-ops, because the v1 rows above produced neither
# name. the lesson the hard way: a shipped row is frozen, always add.
2 31-root 30-root
2 30-proving-this-machine -
